# docdriftfix — the NEGATIVE CONTROL for the dated-record lane

Every date in this file is a date the document TALKS ABOUT, or a freshness stamp claiming the document is
CURRENT. Neither dates the document as a record, so every anchor here must stay in `drift=` and none may
carry `kind="dated-record"`. Getting this wrong is the failure that matters: a false record HIDES real rot.

Last updated: 2026-01-15 — a liveness claim, which is the opposite of a record.
Written up after the 2026-01-15 migration, which is a date this file discusses rather than its own.

